WEBVTT

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.970
Seeking out a single ray of light,
hito-suji no hikari wo motome

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:34.210
All I can do is wander on, no matter how far.
hitasura doko made mo tada samayou

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:42.950
As I breathe a sigh not unlike surrender,
akirame ni nita tameiki wo tsuki-nagara

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:52.270
I don't want to fear how I've been hurt, all the time.
kizutsuku koto wo osoretaku nai yo itsu mo

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.650
Set me free now!

00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:01.060
Come on, let it all go, to the far reaches of time,
saa tokihanate subete toki no kanata ni

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:01.080
From that which binds the soul!
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:06.910
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo
From that which binds the soul!

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.200
For my heartbeat!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.690
Make freedom your weapon,
jiyuu wo buki ni

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:11.760
And you are sure to attain it!
kitto te ni ireru no yo

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.470
kitto te ni ireru no yo
And you are sure to attain it!

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:15.510
The power to believe and dream is there
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:21.590
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo
The power to believe and dream is there

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:21.630
for you to go on living.
ikite yuku tame ni

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.960
ikite yuku tame ni
for you to go on living.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:36.670
You keep yourself on edge like that for too long and you'll ruin your health.

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.340
I guess they describe it as making any sign that you're still alive disappear.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:43.880
The way how, without noticing it, you don't even realize how you usually are.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.050
Aren't you... the plucky one?

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.760
Here.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:09.310
Eat it now. Once they come on out, it'll be too late for regrets.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:11.320
So when exactly did all this come about?

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.320
Well, let's see...

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:16.340
It's been like this for as long as I can remember, anyhow.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:21.320
I believe they first appeared about 15 years or so ago.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:21.980
Keith!

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.120
Well, where's the harm?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.320
He can't help that he's just woken up!

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.990
Let's at least tell him that much!

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.620
We have not received any instructions to do so.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.660
Now hurry and relieve Minnie at sentry.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:39.580
Hell, the operation doesn't go as planned, and the elites get all snippy.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:40.600
Right, right.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.740
Yes, ma'am

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.620
Operation?

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:52.950
The plan was really for us to recover everyone while you were all still sleeping.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:57.830
But the Blue around the installation suddenly became active...

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.960
A zero harvest would have gotten even us abandoned by those over us.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.300
We were lucky to have gotten even one of you.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:07.630
Lucky?

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:08.970
Huh?

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.640
Lucky, you say?

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.650
Getting woken up out of the blue, not realizing what has happening?

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:18.310
Nearly getting killed, without even knowing what was going on!?

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:21.650
That's what you call lucky!? Why!?

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:24.990
When the hell did I ever ask to be awakened!?

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:28.890
Given this situation, don't you think I'd have rather slept through it?

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:33.190
Is this you guys' idea of helping me out? Well!?

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:36.000
Stop yelling. They'll find us.

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.330
So what if they do!?

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.500
How can you be so calm about all this?

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:45.700
How can you understand how it feels for me to have been awakened all alone?

00:05:53.050 --> 00:06:00.010
The first time the existence of the Blue was confirmed was in 2017 by the western calendar.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.820
Fourteen years ago now.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:08.500
At first, it was thought that they were a biological weapon that some country had developed.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:10.000
But they were different.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:27.720
Their very ecology utterly shattered all conceptions held about biology up to that point.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.190
They fed not only on organic matter,

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:33.160
but inorganic matter as well, converting it to functional energy.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:37.490
In an era when material civilization was at its peak,

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.550
this world must have been an optimal feeding ground for them.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:46.500
It was a simple matter for them to turn the Earth into a planet of death,

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:48.160
almost in the blink of an eye.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.740
I suppose to them, humans must have been tantamount to insects,

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.640
crawling over what they were feeding on.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:59.240
Since humans amounted to only a meager source of energy for them,

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.740
they wrap us up like dumplings, like that,

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:05.620
and feed on us once they've assembled a large enough number.

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:13.030
But the Blue do more than just multiply.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:18.060
After each time we humans attack them, they evolve over and over to protect themselves.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.710
The battle has become prolonged...

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:26.370
Gradually, as people started running out of places to run,

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:31.110
we fled the world the Blue had turned into their nesting grounds and escaped into space.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.310
To space?

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:42.520
Up beyond the sky, above our orbiting satellites, is a space station named "Second Earth."

00:07:53.370 --> 00:08:01.010
Team Gran Seil, Access Code FE-2035-C. Operation name "Cytokine"

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:05.410
Collating recovered sample. Kaido Yuji, E-D carrier.

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:09.720
Began Sleep treatment at National Immunity Laboratories in 2009.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.960
Further, due to increased Blue activity,

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:21.560
excepting Kaido Yuji, the facility's entire Sleeper population was lost.

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:36.010
Request instructions concerning rendezvous point with recovery vehicle.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:44.250
Our location is JP E-204. There are seven in our party.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:47.260
Standard platoon outfitting.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:52.250
The surviving humans organized themselves into combat units to resist the Blue.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:56.600
The higher command began research on how to exterminate the Blue.

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:03.600
And in 2031, Second Earth finally began operations to take back the Earth.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.270
And you're saying that saving me is part of all this?

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:13.940
Saving you? You just happen to be one of the samples we recovered by chance.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.610
You've got it all backward.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:18.280
Sam... ple?

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:21.310
Our duty now is to wait for a recovery vehicle to arrive,

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:25.300
then return via spaceport to the space station.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.960
Have you heard quite enough yet?

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:31.930
Quite enough? By chance, you say?

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:36.910
How can that be? How did an order like that come down?

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:41.640
Why is it necessary for you to take an ordinary guy like myself into space with you?

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:45.710
That has nothing to do with my duty. I don't care.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.990
You've gone too far!

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.350
I went to sleep in order to cure my illness.

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.980
Why couldn't you just leave me be!?

00:09:54.030 --> 00:10:01.990
If I'd known this is how it would turn out, I... I...

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:04.520
...you would have rather died?

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:11.470
They're coming!

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.680
If you want to die, I won't stop you.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.980
But my job is to get you back to the station.

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.390
Until then, you'll have to stay alive on me.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:48.980
System Check?

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:50.670
We'll have to take our chances.

00:11:58.080 --> 00:11:59.070
Still...

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:55.800
It's been 22 years that I've slept.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:03.310
It's an age where normally, it wouldn't be unusual if my mom or dad were still alive.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:15.180
Nah. But knowing him?

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:22.530
Even now, he's sure to be off somewhere...

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.990
Why this airport in particular?

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:33.660
Up to now, there's been no confirmation that there are any seagoing Blue.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:35.000
At sea,

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:38.700
...all we have to worry about are Blue attacking from the air.

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:43.340
There's no time.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:46.580
Stuff the cargo carrier in as-is!

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:59.990
What are we, luggage too?

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:11.970
What's that?

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:20.110
Sleepers that have been recovered from other areas.

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:25.050
There were a number of similar facilities all over Japan, after all.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:27.060
Hey, stop the car!

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:27.990
Now!

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.330
Wait! Where are you going!?

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:39.000
I'm not the only one! I wasn't the only one who was brought here after all!

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:45.870
Go!

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:48.910
What?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.530
W- what!?

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:08.660
Impossible!

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:12.900
A Blue!?

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.280
Shit!

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.910
What the hell's going on!?

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:37.960
Oh no! Malcolm, hurry to the trailer!

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.060
How are they coming from the sea!?

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:56.680
Damn him!

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:58.050
What are you waiting for!?

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:01.350
Yeah! I've got to wake everyone up!

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.960
What the hell are you dinking around for!?

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.970
The trailer's lurching around so much, I can't get us out of here!

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:22.300
Wake up! Wake up, I say! Wake up!

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:25.640
Hey! Hurry up, or you'll all be dead!

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:28.300
What are you doing!? Get over here!

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:33.650
No way! I've had enough of being alone in this kind of place!

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:35.310
Please...

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:38.010
...I don't care who, just wake up!

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:52.030
I'm telling you it's hopeless. We can't resuscitate them here.

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:55.170
Come on!

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:32.300
Dammit! Why's this taking so long?

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:35.070
Joey! Get us closer to it!

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:39.640
If we can't shoot it, we can use the arms on this thing to smash its thorax directly!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:41.650
You've gotta be kidding!

00:18:41.690 --> 00:18:43.980
Never mind, just do it!

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:44.510
Of all the...!

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:15.850
Get in!

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:49.110
Hey! W- wait a minute!

00:19:57.690 --> 00:20:01.560
It can't... It can't be...

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:25.820
How can it be!? They came through an underwater pipe!

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:31.360
...Keith...

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:03.320
If I'd known this, maybe I would have rather died...

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:09.030
But... I wouldn't want to get killed without a fight! Not to them!

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:39.990
Although the days when we smiled again and again
hohoemi kasaneta hibi ga

00:21:41.350 --> 00:21:46.120
Have passed away into dreams,
maboroshi ni natte mo

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:55.270
I will surely not lose my way.
watashi wa kitto mayowanai

00:21:55.390 --> 00:22:01.440
To go on to the future,
mirai ni yuku tame ni

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:07.860
To become an adult,
otona ni naru tame ni

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:15.050
I again recall now the memories
mogaite kita omoide wo kokoro de

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:20.210
twisting in my heart.
ima wa kurikaesu

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:26.270
I'm living in one time,
hitotsu no toki wo iki

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:32.550
While choosing two dreams,
futatsu no yume erabi

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:40.030
And love taught me what it means...
soshite ai ga oshiete kureta yo ne

00:22:40.210 --> 00:22:46.890
to cherish someone.
hito wo omou imi

00:22:52.590 --> 00:22:53.680
No way!

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:56.250
There's no way I'm going to get myself killed by one of those bug-like things,

00:22:56.290 --> 00:22:59.290
not while I'm unable to do anything about it!

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:02.890
I'm not going to just be baggage!

00:23:02.930 --> 00:23:06.890
I won't beg for help, or be treated like a baby any longer!

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:09.910
And so... I will fight!

00:23:09.940 --> 00:23:13.210
So please, tell me what I need to know to live!
